{"record": "turn", "turn": 4, "seconds": 6.63, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["thinking", "tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11268, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 961, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_01RDQQw6fqDbqF7DfNYLzTgx", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "No. The dSph gamma-ray limit uses a one-sided 95% threshold: 2[ln L_max − ln L(σv_95)] = 2.71 (TS drop of 2.71, or 1.355 in ln L). It profiles over the per-dwarf J-factor normalization, with a Gaussian prior in log10 s from the J-factor uncertainty, over log10 s in [-3, 3]. The AMS-02 antiproton limit uses ΔQ = 3.84 (Q = -2lnL), the upper endpoint of the 95% interval for one parameter of interest. The paper says this differs from the usual one-sided 2.71. It profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, with a Gaussian penalty in log10 L centered at 4.96 kpc with σ = 0.197, over 1 ≤ L/kpc ≤ 12.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261120T080300Z_dev-02_staged_578c", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "No. The dSph gamma-ray limit uses a one-sided 95% threshold: 2[ln L_max − ln L(σv_95)] = 2.71 (TS drop of 2.71, or 1.355 in ln L). It profiles over the per-dwarf J-factor normalization, with a Gaussian prior in log10 s from the J-factor uncertainty, over log10 s in [-3, 3]. The AMS-02 antiproton limit uses ΔQ = 3.84 (Q = -2lnL), the upper endpoint of the 95% interval for one parameter of interest. The paper says this differs from the usual one-sided 2.71. It profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, with a Gaussian penalty in log10 L centered at 4.96 kpc with σ = 0.197, over 1 ≤ L/kpc ≤ 12.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 11.893, "tool_calls": 4, "tool_result_chars": 19594, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1281, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 26628, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-20T08:03:12+00:00"}
